{
  "info": {
    "name": "14 \u00b7 Metrics & analytics",
    "description": "The analytics reads \u2014 whole-event and per-evaluation metrics \u2014 and the metrics-access level that gates them (a separate axis from group visibility).\n\n**Flow.** Setup publishes three admin-owned groups differing only in `metrics_access_during` / `access_level`, plus one evaluation. A) owner reads the group aggregate (`scope: full`) and the evaluation slice; B) the gating, probed by the visible non-owner `viewer`: `inherit_group_access` \u2192 200, `owner_only` \u2192 403 (visible but not permitted; the owner still gets 200), `invitation_only` \u2192 404 (**visibility gates first** \u2014 no existence leak); C) no-token 401.\n\n**No dbshell needed** \u2014 every gating state is reachable through group config (`metrics_access_during`, `access_level`) plus the lifecycle (`approve` \u2192 `publish`), so the collection is fully API-driven.\n\n**Not covered here:** the `members_personal_metrics` **personal-scope** read (a member seeing only their own contributions) needs a provisioned, activated group member with `view_personal_metrics` \u2014 the same manual-token onboarding as `07`/`10` \u2014 so it's left out of this self-contained collection. `metrics_access_after` (applied once a group is `inactive`) is likewise deferred.\n\n**Auth model.** Per-request: `{{admin_token}}` (owner) and `{{viewer_token}}` (visible non-owner), `noauth` for 401. Self-contained \u2014 no `00-bootstrap`, no manual token.\n\n**Publish gate.** Publishing needs at least one live evaluation, each carrying a scenario, so every fixture group gets an evaluation + scenario between its approve and its publish \u2014 not only the Inherit group whose evaluation-level metrics folder A reads.\n\n**Leftovers.** The three groups leak (no group DELETE; `run_suffix` keeps them unique); Teardown deletes all three evaluations.\n\n**Verified:** 31/31 against a live stack, twice (`make up` + `make seedlocal`).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "noauth"
  },
